  <h2>What we publish</h2>
  <p>Each edition delivers one deep analysis and two concise signals. We focus on research at the edge of human vitality: quantum biology, cellular senolytics, NRF-2 activation, brain connectomics, and daily functional health.</p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>Our intelligence pipeline monitors preprints (arXiv, bioRxiv, medRxiv), clinical trial databases, and leading scientific journals. We screen candidates through a high-signal novelty filter to eliminate repetitive advice and isolate break-through findings.</p>

  <p>Every brief explicitly cites and links its original sources. Agewell Brief adds context, biophysical framing, and practical takeaways—never aggregated clickbait.</p>

  <h2 id="editorial-desk">The editorial desk</h2>
  <p><strong>Agewell Brief Editorial Desk</strong> reflects a rigorous, multi-layer process of automated retrieval, assisted drafting, human review, and publication under unified editorial accountability.</p>

  <h2>What we believe</h2>
  <p>Aging is not an inevitable decline into medical dependency. Our readers are capable adults with sharp judgment and vast potential ahead. We write accordingly: direct science, original sources, and empowering clarity.</p>
